        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int (\\frac{1}{8x+8}+\\frac{1}{8x+6})\\,\\text{d}x.$ Assume that $K$ is an arbitrary positive constant.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's solve this using the general formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{8x+8}+\\frac{1}{8x+6})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{8x+8}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{8x+6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|8x+8|+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|8x+6|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|(8x+8)(8x+6)|+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061K \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(K|(8x+8)(8x+6)|)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the laws of logarithms to write the result as a single logarithm.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
